From: Copilot <223556219+Copilot@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Tue, 23 Jun 2026 15:21:00 +0800
Subject: [PATCH 2/2] media: ipu7: sync ACPI csi2 config with ep-aware isys ABI

The IPU7 "get source pad according to csi2 ep fwnode" change extends
struct ipu7_isys_csi2_config with a new fwnode endpoint pointer:

    struct fwnode_handle *ep;

However, the ACPI/platform-data side still defines and allocates the older
shorter ipu_isys_csi2_config without that field. When the patched IPU7
isys code reads csi2->ep on the ACPI path it reads beyond the end of the
allocated object and may pass garbage into
fwnode_graph_get_remote_endpoint(), leading to a rare fresh-boot OOPS.

Synchronize the ACPI-side struct definition with the IPU7-side layout so
the object size matches and ep is zero-initialized on the ACPI path.

Symptom:
- Rare fresh-boot OOPS in fwnode_graph_get_remote_endpoint()
- Non-canonical fwnode pointer observed in the crash log

Root cause:
- ABI/layout mismatch between the IPU7 csi2 config struct and the ACPI
  csi2 config struct after adding the ep field

Solution:
- Add the missing ep field to the ACPI-side struct definition

---
 include/media/ipu-acpi.h | 1 +
 1 file changed, 1 insertion(+)

diff --git a/include/media/ipu-acpi.h b/include/media/ipu-acpi.h
index 0000000000000..0000000000000 100644
--- a/include/media/ipu-acpi.h
+++ b/include/media/ipu-acpi.h
@@ -31,6 +31,7 @@ struct ipu_isys_csi2_config {
 	unsigned int nlanes;
 	unsigned int port;
 	enum v4l2_mbus_type bus_type;
+	struct fwnode_handle *ep;
 };
 
 struct ipu_isys_subdev_i2c_info {
